ting. I need to regenerate `temp_melted` without the 'ObjectId' column.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"0e699b38","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1755507890690,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":2092,"user":{"displayName":"Houd Lillian Maltiti","userId":"14324335200633603992"}},"outputId":"de9d24c3-ab00-428d-dd06-edb54af86b8f"},"source":["# Filter for temperature change indicator with the correct name\n","temp_df = df_west_africa[df_west_africa['Indicator'] == 'Temperature change with respect to a baseline climatology, corresponding to the period 1951-1980']\n","\n","# Define the year columns, excluding 'ObjectId'\n","year_cols = [col for col in temp_df.columns if col.startswith('F') and col[1:].isdigit()]\n","\n","# Melt the DataFrame to long format, specifying id_vars and value_vars\n","temp_melted = temp_df.melt(id_vars=['Country', 'ISO2', 'ISO3', 'Indicator', 'Unit', 'Source', 'CTS_Code', 'CTS_Name', 'CTS_Full_Descriptor'],\n","                           value_vars=year_cols,\n","                           var_name='Year', value_name='Temperature')\n","\n","# Extract year from the 'Year' column (remove 'F')\n","temp_melted['Year'] = temp_melted['Year'].str.replace('F', '').astype(int)\n","\n","# Get the list of unique countries\n","countries = temp_melted['Country'].unique()\n","\n","# Iterate through each country and create a plot\n","for country in countries:\n","    # Filter data for the current country\n","    country_temp_df = temp_melted[temp_melted['Country'] == country]\n","\n","    # Plot temperature trend for the country\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","    plt.plot(country_temp_df['Year'], country_temp_df['Temperature'], marker='o')\n","    plt.title(f'Temperature Trend in {country}')\n","    plt.xlabel('Year')\n","    plt.ylabel('Temperature (°C or anomaly)')\n","    plt.grid(True)\n","    plt.show()"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dc93b756"},"source":["##**Compare country trends**\n","\n","### Subtask:\n","Consider visualizing the trends of multiple countries on the same plot for comparison."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"78683cc2"},"source":["**Reasoning**:\n","Create a single plot to visualize the temperature trends for all Western African countries for comparison.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":160},"id":"40578b3b","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1755507919175,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":819,"user":{"displayName":"Houd Lillian Maltiti","userId":"14324335200633603992"}},"outputId":"2a76244d-f750-41ab-8dac-43e56f1a5299"},"source":["# Create a single figure for the combined plot\n","plt.figure(figsize=(15, 8))\n","\n","# Iterate through each unique country and plot its temperature trend\n","countries = temp_melted['Country'].unique()\n","for country in countries:\n","    country_temp_df = temp_melted[temp_melted['Country'] == country]\n","    plt.plot(country_temp_df['Year'], country_temp_df['Temperature'], marker='o', label=country)\n","\n","# Add title and labels\n","plt.title(\"Temperature Trends in Western African Countries (1961-2022)\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Year\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Temperature Anomaly (°C)\")\n","\n","# Include legend and grid\n","plt.legend(title=\"Country\", bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","\n","# Display the combined plot\n","plt.show()"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1500x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"170e5550"},"source":["##**Analysis and interpretation (SUMMARY)📉**\n","\n","### Subtask:\n","Discuss the observed temperature trends for individual countries and compare them to the regional average."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2a274a6a"},"source":["Based on the individual country plots and the combined plot showing temperature trends in Western African Countries from 1961 to 2022, we can observe the following:\n","\n","*  **Overall Warming Trend:** The plots clearly indicate a general warming trend across most of the Western African countries included in this analysis over the observed period. While there are year-to-year fluctuations in temperature anomalies, the long-term trajectory shows an increase in temperature relative to the 1951-1980 baseline.\n","*   **Variations Across Countries:** Although the overall trend is warming, the rate and magnitude of temperature increase vary among the different countries. Some countries appear to experience more significant warming than others, and the year-to-year variability also differs. The individual country plots allow us to see these specific variations.\n","*   **Fluctuations and Anomalies:** The plots show considerable year-to-year fluctuations in temperature anomalies. There are periods where temperatures are significantly above or below the baseline, highlighting the natural variability of climate in addition to the long-term warming trend.\n","*   **Comparison of Trends:** The combined plot allows for a visual comparison of the temperature trends across all the included Western African countries. This plot makes it easier to see similarities and differences in the warming patterns and the timing of significant temperature shifts.\n","\n","Overall, the visualizations support the conclusion that Western Africa is experiencing a warming trend, consistent with global climate change patterns, but with localized variations across different countries in the region."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"398e8391"},"source":["## **Limitations**\n","\n","It's important to be aware of the limitations of this analysis:\n","\n","*   **Data Availability:** The analysis is limited by the data available in the Climate Change Indicators dataset. As we saw with the CO₂ data for Western Africa, not all indicators might be available for all countries or across the entire time period.\n","*   **Indicator Specificity:** The dataset provides indicators at a national level. A more granular analysis (e.g., regional within countries, or specific cities) would require more detailed data.\n","*   **Baseline Period:** The temperature change is measured with respect to a specific baseline (1951-1980). Choosing a different baseline period could slightly alter the magnitude of the observed anomalies.\n","*   **Causation vs. Correlation:** While we can observe trends and potential relationships between indicators (like temperature and CO₂ if that data were available), this analysis does not prove causation.\n","*   **External Factors:** Climate change is influenced by a multitude of factors. This analysis focuses on a few key indicators and does not encompass all potential drivers or impacts."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Top 10 Facts about Global Climate Change:**\n","\n","* The 10 warmest years on record have all occurred since 2010. (This aligns with the warming trends we've seen in the temperature data.)\n","* Sea levels have risen by about 8-9 inches since 1880, with about a third of that rise occurring in the last 25 years.\n","* Coral reefs are highly vulnerable to warming ocean temperatures and ocean acidification, leading to widespread coral bleaching and ecosystem collapse.\n","* Extreme weather events, such as heatwaves, droughts, floods, and wildfires, have become more frequent and intense in many parts of the world due to climate change.\n","* Renewable energy sources like solar and wind power are becoming increasingly cost-competitive with fossil fuels, offering a significant opportunity to reduce greenhouse gas emissions."],"metadata":{"id":"z9hINmnwgbsd"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ade59850"},"source":["## **Acknowledgment and Reproducibility**\n","\n","This project utilizes the Climate Change Indicators dataset from Kaggle, which is made available under a CC0: Public Domain license. This means the data is freely available for use without copyright restrictions.\n","\n","The analysis conducted in this notebook can be reproduced by following the steps outlined, starting from downloading the dataset using the Kaggle API. The code provided in each cell details the data loading, cleaning, and visualization processes."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##**CSV Below**👇"],"metadata":{"id":"mhW_cDQ4hXzy"}},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"68afe0d9","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1755510031417,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":130,"user":{"displayName":"Houd Lillian Maltiti","userId":"14324335200633603992"}},"outputId":"d120eb1d-59c0-4d78-d87d-e7aeedaaee81"},"source":["# Save the temp_melted DataFrame to a CSV file\n","temp_melted.to_csv('western_africa_temperature_data.csv', index=False)\n","\n","print(\"Saved temp_melted to western_africa_temperature_data.csv\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Saved temp_melted to western_africa_temperature_data.csv\n"]}]}]}